' @startuml Mobile Token Flow <<Seqence Diagram>>

' actor User
' participant MobileApplication as App

' participant nginx
' ' participant oauth2Proxy
' participant Keycloak

' participant NodeJS as "Node.js BFF"
' participant Redis
' participant FHIR
' participant RevocationService
' ==User Registration Flow==
' ' User -> MobileApplication : Registration request 
' ' MobileApplication -> Keycloak : Registration request
' ' Keycloak -> MobileApplication : Accept registration request
' ' MobileApplication -> Keycloak : Submit registration details
' ' Keycloak -> Keycloak : Create user account
' ' MobileApplication -> nginx : Patient profile data form
' ' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward profile data
' User -> App : Registration request 
' ' App -> App : Input registration details in custom form
' App -> nginx : POST /auth/register with credentials
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward to backend
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Create user 
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : User created
' NodeJS -> nginx : 201 Created
' nginx -> App : Registration success
' App -> User : Prompt to sign in
' App -> nginx : POST /api/patient with Bearer token header
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward with Bearer token
' NodeJS -> FHIR : Create user profile resource with token
' FHIR -> NodeJS : Acknowledgment
' NodeJS -> nginx : Acknowledgment
' nginx -> App : Acknowledgment
' App -> User : Display main page



' == User Login Flow ==
' ' User -> MobileApplication : Login request on login page
' ' MobileApplication -> Keycloak : Redirect to auth endpoint (PKCE challenge)
' ' Keycloak -> MobileApplication : Authorization code (Authz code Flow)
' ' MobileApplication -> Keycloak : exchange code for tokens (with PKCE verifier)
' ' Keycloak -> MobileApplication : Access token , Refresh token , ID token
' ' MobileApplication -> MobileApplication : store tokens securely 
' ' MobileApplication -> User : display main page

' User -> App : Login request on login page
' App -> App : Generate code_verifier + code_challenge (PKCE)
' App -> App : Input credentials in custom login form
' App -> nginx : POST /auth/mobile/authorize 
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward to backend 
' NodeJS -> NodeJS : Validate input
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Authenticate user 
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : User authenticated
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Create authorization code bound to code_challenge
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : Authorization code 
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Exchange code with code_verifier + client_secret
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : Access token, Refresh token, ID token
' NodeJS -> nginx : Return tokens to client
' nginx -> App : Return tokens
' App -> App : Store tokens securely (Keystore)
' App -> User : Display main page

' == User Action Requiring Data (API Call) ==
' ' User -> MobileApplication : Action that needs Data
' ' MobileApplication -> nginx : API call with token

' User -> App : Action that needs Data
' App -> nginx : API call with Authorization: Bearer token header
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward request with Bearer token
' NodeJS -> NodeJS : Validate Bearer token signature (JWT)

' alt Access token valid
'     ' NodeJS -> NodeJS : Validate Bearer token signature (JWT)
'     alt Resource available in cache
'         NodeJS -> Redis : Get resource from cache
'         Redis -> NodeJS : Resource
'     else Resource not in cache
'         NodeJS -> FHIR : Request resource with Access token
'         FHIR -> NodeJS : Resource
'         NodeJS -> Redis : Store resource in cache
'         Redis -> NodeJS : Ack
'     end
'     NodeJS -> nginx : Response with data
'     nginx -> App : Response containing data
'     App -> User : Display data



' else Access token expired
'     App -> App : Detect expiry locally
'     App -> nginx : POST /auth/mobile/refresh with refresh_token in body
'     nginx -> NodeJS : Forward refresh request
'     NodeJS -> Keycloak : Use refresh token to obtain new tokens
'     Keycloak -> NodeJS : New Access token, Refresh token, ID token
'     NodeJS -> nginx : Return new access_token + refresh_token
'     nginx -> App : Return tokens
'     App -> App : Store new tokens securely (Keychain/Keystore)
'     App -> nginx : Retry API call with new Bearer token
' end

' == Logout Flow (Mobile — Per-session) ==

' ' User -> MobileApplication : Tap "Sign out"
' ' MobileApplication -> nginx : POST /auth/logout { sessionId or accessToken }
' ' nginx -> NodeJS : /auth/logout -> call RevocationService
' ' RevocationService -> Redis : DEL oauth2_proxy:session:<id>
' ' RevocationService -> Keycloak : POST /protocol/openid-connect/revoke (token) 
' ' NodeJS -> MobileApplication : 200 OK
' ' MobileApplication -> User : Signed out (this device)

' User -> App : Tap "Logout"
' App -> nginx : POST /auth/logout with refresh_token in body
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward logout request
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Revoke refresh token
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : Token revoked
' NodeJS -> nginx : 200 OK
' nginx -> App : 200 OK
' App -> App : Clear stored tokens from Keystore
' App -> User : Return to login screen

' == Logout Flow (Mobile — Global across all devices) ==
' User -> App : Tap "Logout of all devices"
' App -> nginx : POST /auth/logout-all with refresh_token
' nginx -> NodeJS : Forward logout-all request
' NodeJS -> Keycloak : Admin logout user (invalidate refresh tokens / sessions)
' Keycloak -> NodeJS : Logout completed
' NodeJS -> nginx : 200 OK
' nginx -> App : Logout complete
' App -> App : Clear stored tokens from Keystore
' App -> User : All sessions signed out

' ' MobileApplication -> Keycloak : use refresh token to obtain new tokens
' ' Keycloak -> MobileApplication : new Access token , new Refresh token , new ID token
' ' MobileApplication -> nginx : API call with new Access token
' @enduml
